WEBVTT

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:03.490
広げる

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:06.440
Thank you!

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:07.380
Thank you for watching!

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:33.340
Peace.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.550
What? Two skulls sleeping?

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:09.330
Hehehe, I won again, no regrets.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:14.190
Ah, Henrique, come play a little with us, just to vary.

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:29.040
Hear the voice of God, obey, and know that at the right time you will find salvation.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:33.760
Yagami, are you paying attention?

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:37.150
Can you please translate the following sentence?

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:43.970
Follow the teachings of God and receive the blessings.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:45.130
So it will be.

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:47.540
And the seas will be abundant again,

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:50.380
and the furious storms will calm down.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:53.700
Today, approximately at 11 a.m.,

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:56.100
a 32-year-old man was found dead,

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:58.400
stabbed in his apartment in Yokohama,

00:02:59.060 --> 00:02:59.400
Kanagawa Province.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:02.700
Take care of this murder.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:09.320
In today's local news, the suspect of the murder, Naoki Kofuji, was arrested in the Shibuya district, Tokyo.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:17.190
He is under custody, accused of the brutal murder of his partner, who was only 25 years old when she was killed.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:25.420
Day in, day out, the same news repeats itself.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:27.440
That's it.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:33.450
This world is rotten.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:42.480
Another consequence is the extinction of various species of the planet.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:44.800
I don't believe it. Did you pay to see this?

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:45.800
And I don't know what you gave me in the box.

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:49.560
Nowadays, the number of species in extinction is the largest ever recorded.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:25.620
Death Note

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:33.440
The way to use it.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:36.440
The human whose name is written on this notebook

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:37.560
will die.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:43.610
Hm, hm, this is ridiculous.

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:46.030
Not to mention it's morbid.

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:49.880
It's not very different from those pyramids you get by e-mail.

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:53.520
The human whose name is written on this notebook will die.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.060
It's been a while.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.760
There must be something wrong with me to guess that.

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:15.580
This notebook will not work unless you have in mind the face of the person whose name is being written.

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:18.920
Therefore, another person with the same name will not be affected.

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:26.600
If the cause of death is written up to 40 seconds after the person's name according to the human time unit, this will be done.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:29.850
If the cause of death is not specified, the person will die of a...

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:36.020
After the cause, the death details must be provided in the next 6 minutes and 40 seconds.

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:41.900
So, depending on the person you have in mind, you can kill him easily or with pain.

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:44.330
This is too detailed to be a joke.

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:55.800
So I write the person's name and she dies.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:58.390
As if someone believed that.

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:19.060
If someone really dies, does that make me a killer?

00:06:21.630 --> 00:06:23.510
Okay, that's totally impossible.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.660
again, making 8 people hostages in a creche.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:34.920
The hostages include children and babysitters.

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:39.480
The police identified the suspect as being Kuro Otoharada, 42 years old,

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:40.440
currently unemployed.

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:42.920
We hope negotiations begin soon.

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:51.760
A cardiac arrest in 40 seconds. Let's see.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:54.900
At this moment, that's all the police reveals.

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:58.640
We're all worried about the safety of these hostages.

00:06:59.220 --> 00:06:59.680
You're right.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.630
We will continue to monitor the situation here.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:06.230
Thank you for the news. What do you think of this, Mr. Hashimoto?

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:09.840
Well, we can only expect a quick solution to this situation.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:13.540
It seems that the notebook does not work.

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:16.770
Well, I did not expect it to work.

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:21.660
Wait, we're seeing something. It seems that there is movement in the front door.

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:24.910
They are leaving and they seem helpless.

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:27.970
The special forces are in action and they will come in.

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:29.890
We do not know if the suspect was...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.180
Huh? I know. Okay, now we have confirmation. The suspect was found dead in there.

00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:37.260
I repeat, the suspect is dead.

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:37.980
Dead?

00:07:41.900 --> 00:07:45.200
Special forces deny the allegations and shot the suspect.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:48.220
So you think he was shot and committed suicide?

00:07:48.990 --> 00:07:52.090
Well, according to the witnesses, the suspect had a fuming attack.

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:58.220
A cardiac arrest? I don't believe it.

00:07:59.000 --> 00:07:59.560
It's a coincidence.

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:01.850
It can only be a coincidence.

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:06.340
It's half past nine, you know?

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.000
Don't you have class tonight?

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:10.750
I do! I'll be ready soon.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:16.520
It's unlikely, but if this is real,

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:18.700
I have to try again.

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:21.820
And in this case, it's better to be another criminal.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:25.620
But if he's very well known, I'll have problems.

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:29.980
If he dies, there's a good chance the news about his death...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.300
be covered and I have to see the results soon.

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:35.130
Hey, friend!

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:37.160
What's up, Sudo?

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:39.520
Didn't you say you'd lend me 2,000 yen?

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:42.600
What? Again? Can't I do that?

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:44.860
Sudo, I think I should try to kill this guy.

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:47.940
No, it's better to avoid killing people I know.

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:51.730
Hey, but does it really matter?

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:56.660
Would anyone care if a guy like him disappeared one day?

00:08:59.360 --> 00:08:59.660
Cool!

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.240
I think we'll go to the mall after school.

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:04.910
Look, we're going to have a bachelor party tomorrow.

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:05.710
Do you want to come?

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:06.420
Of course!

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:08.360
Oh, I'm not going to lose for nothing.

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:10.640
Damn, why is my mom so useless?

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:12.760
She never came to pick me up on time.

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:15.840
When you start looking around,

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:19.400
you wonder if you would do society a favor

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:21.240
by getting rid of all these people.

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:25.080
Hey, kitty!

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:27.000
Where are you going?

00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:28.140
Come have fun with us!

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:29.560
This is Otaku.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.820
It's a nice place a mile away.

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:35.540
Hey, kitty. I'm Otaku Shibuimaru.

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:37.000
What do you think?

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:39.080
Come hang out with us, kitty.

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:41.120
Please, I don't want a problem.

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:43.460
See? He doesn't want a problem.

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:44.820
Isn't he cute?

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:51.830
Come on, guys. Take your clothes off.

00:09:51.850 --> 00:09:52.730
What? Are you sure?

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:55.290
No! Stop it!

00:09:55.850 --> 00:09:56.410
Please!

00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:06.380
And now, what is going to happen?

00:10:08.530 --> 00:10:09.010
Ouch!

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:22.920
It's real!

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:32.740
Xavi

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:35.110
It's better to go walking.

00:10:56.870 --> 00:10:57.510
It's been five days.

00:10:59.270 --> 00:10:59.770
So...

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:01.730
It's better if I go in.

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:04.340
Huh? Are you going somewhere, Luke?

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.700
I'm sorry, but that's the way our world is.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:12.050
True, but I lost my Death Note.

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:15.680
You messed it up, didn't you?

00:11:16.220 --> 00:11:17.310
Give me a break.

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:20.090
Haven't you sung the old man to have a second book?

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:21.740
Don't tell me you lost both.

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:25.420
You must have some idea where you left this thing.

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:26.200
What?

00:11:59.310 --> 00:11:59.530
No

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.340
I wasn't expecting you home so early.

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:06.520
Yeah. Hi, Mom. It's because, uh...

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:10.840
Oh, the test results, right?

00:12:11.240 --> 00:12:12.200
I've been waiting all day.

00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:16.810
Congratulations. The first one again.

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:19.080
It's the highest score you've ever had.

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:21.610
Yeah, I think so. I'm going to study in my room.

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:22.730
Don't interrupt me, okay? Please.

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:24.080
Who knows?

00:12:24.440 --> 00:12:27.880
Oh, Light. Do you want anything, honey?

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:29.220
You can ask for whatever you want.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.600
No, it's all right, mom. Thank you.

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:36.390
I already have what I want.

00:12:51.980 --> 00:12:57.840
I see you got the taste for the...

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:00.680
FU-

00:13:05.850 --> 00:13:07.010
Why were you so surprised?

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:09.960
Yoso Ushinigami Ryuki.

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:11.600
This notebook was mine.

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:17.270
Judging by your laughter, you have already discovered that what you have in your hand is not an ordinary notebook.

00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:25.490
Shinigami

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:27.620
A God of Death.

00:13:28.630 --> 00:13:29.610
Subtitles by the Amara.org community

00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:30.660
I'm not surprised.

00:13:31.590 --> 00:13:32.030
Isn't it true?

00:13:33.510 --> 00:13:34.070
I was...

00:13:35.050 --> 00:13:35.770
waiting for you

00:13:36.550 --> 00:13:37.130
Ryuki

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:42.070
I've already found out that this notebook is real.

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:43.910
And it didn't even take long.

00:13:44.870 --> 00:13:46.910
And now that I witness the proof of your power,

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:49.860
I just feel more confident in what I'm going to do.

00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:51.610
How interesting!

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:53.780
I wasn't expecting this.

00:13:55.300 --> 00:13:58.180
Several Death Notes reached the human world in the past.

00:13:58.760 --> 00:13:59.960
But you are the first to forget.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:05.110
so many names. Look how many people you've killed in just five days.

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:08.070
Most of them would be reluctant to write so much.

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:13.890
I've already prepared, Ryuki. I used the notebook even knowing it belonged to a Shinigami.

00:14:14.050 --> 00:14:19.560
And now that this Shinigami has arrived, what will happen to me? Will it take my soul?

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:25.110
Hmph. What do you mean? Is this some fantasy you humans invented?

00:14:26.120 --> 00:14:28.220
I'm not going to do anything to you.

00:14:28.650 --> 00:14:28.950
Hmph.

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:34.600
The notebook becomes part of the human world when it touches the Earth.

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:37.300
In other words, the notebook is now yours.

00:14:38.610 --> 00:14:39.730
Is it... mine?

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:42.560
If you don't want to, just give it to someone else.

00:14:43.300 --> 00:14:47.660
But if you do, I'll have to erase your notebook memories.

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:52.580
So you're saying I can use the Death Note whenever I want and I won't be punished?

00:14:53.360 --> 00:14:54.120
Let's say so.

00:14:54.440 --> 00:14:59.280
You'll feel the fear and pain that only the humans who used the notebook know.

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:06.960
And when it's your time to die, he'll come to me so I can write your name on my Death Note.

00:15:07.140 --> 00:15:14.050
I swear that no human who used the Death Note could go to heaven or hell for eternity.

00:15:14.670 --> 00:15:24.930
That's all you have to wait for after death.

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:28.370
Light?

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:32.060
No problem. You can open it.

00:15:35.090 --> 00:15:35.510
What's up?

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:38.900
I thought you'd like the apples the neighbors brought.

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:41.550
Why is it so dark in your room?

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:43.730
It'll ruin your view.

00:15:43.950 --> 00:15:44.650
What's going on?

00:15:45.360 --> 00:15:46.620
Can't my mom see it?

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:52.100
That notebook you found belonged to me.

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:56.570
And since you're using it now, you're the only one who can see me.

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:59.460
Of course, my voice can only be heard by you.

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:05.830
In other words, Death Note is the link between Light, the human, and Ryuki, the Shinigami.

00:16:07.060 --> 00:16:07.580
Delicious.

00:16:11.260 --> 00:16:12.640
I just have one more question to ask.

00:16:12.980 --> 00:16:15.380
Why was I chosen for this?

00:16:16.170 --> 00:16:18.260
Hey, are you listening to me?

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:23.900
In the world of humans, they talk about travel.

00:16:24.220 --> 00:16:26.040
What's the best way to describe it?

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:27.600
Succulent?

00:16:27.820 --> 00:16:29.020
Answer my question.

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:33.620
I didn't choose you. Don't you see? This was an accident.

00:16:34.040 --> 00:16:37.360
Did you really think you had been chosen because you're so smart?

00:16:37.980 --> 00:16:43.460
Don't be so lazy. He fell here by chance, and by chance you caught him.

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:50.060
That's all. That's why I wrote the instructions in English, the most popular language in the human world.

00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:54.530
So why did you leave the notebook? You even wrote the specific instructions.

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:56.770
So don't tell me this was an accident.

00:16:57.410 --> 00:16:58.530
Are you asking me why?

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:00.980
I did that because I was bored.

00:17:03.400 --> 00:17:03.840
Bored?

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:08.480
Shinigami don't have much to do nowadays.

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:11.860
Most of the time, we either cuddle or play.

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:15.970
If you take the time to write names in your Death Note,

00:17:16.090 --> 00:17:18.190
the others laugh at you for working too hard.

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:20.690
If you write the name of another Shinigami,

00:17:20.770 --> 00:17:22.330
it's no use because they don't die.

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:25.400
And since we live in the world of Shinigamis,

00:17:25.460 --> 00:17:27.980
it's also not fun to kill in the world of humans.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:33.020
So I thought it would be more fun if I came here personally.

00:17:33.580 --> 00:17:38.630
I'm surprised by all the names you wrote,

00:17:38.770 --> 00:17:41.160
but I want to know why you wrote the cause of death

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:43.120
only of that guy who was hit by the truck.

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:46.930
If you don't write the cause of death, the victim dies of cardiac arrest.

00:17:47.150 --> 00:17:50.710
And that must be the best thing about Death Note, Ryuki.

00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:51.160
Huh?

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:55.600
Did you know I've already researched the list of the biggest criminals in the world?

00:17:55.740 --> 00:17:58.090
And one day I'm going to get rid of all of them.

00:17:58.330 --> 00:17:59.980
And what's the point of f-

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:00.500
to do that.

00:18:00.730 --> 00:18:04.930
It's a matter of time until they find out that these criminals are being eliminated by someone.

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:07.850
I want the world to know my existence

00:18:09.050 --> 00:18:11.990
Let them know that there is someone out there judging the wicked.

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:14.990
Why worry?

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:15.730
Bye!

00:18:16.250 --> 00:18:18.330
Who wants to win by playing all of them?

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:19.970
Why do you care?

00:18:21.690 --> 00:18:22.170
Because...

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:24.680
I was bored too.

00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:28.960
I wasn't ready to believe.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.940
But now it's obvious.

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:35.270
There's something in Death Note that makes humans want to try at least once.

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:39.530
I killed both of them.

00:18:39.530 --> 00:18:41.900
I... I killed two men!

00:18:42.790 --> 00:18:44.700
Those were human lives.

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:49.490
This will not be forgotten. Besides, who am I to judge people?

00:18:50.670 --> 00:18:56.650
No, no, no. Maybe I was wrong.

00:18:57.380 --> 00:18:59.420
That's exactly what I was thinking.

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:04.120
This world is rotten, and those who make it rot deserve to die.

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:06.940
Someone has to do this, so why not me?

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:13.760
Even if I have to sacrifice my mind and soul, it's worth it, because the world can't go on like this.

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:19.570
What would happen if someone else took this notebook?

00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:24.090
Is there anyone else out there besides me who wants to eliminate the worms of the world?

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:27.200
If I don't do that, who's going to do it?

00:19:28.010 --> 00:19:28.910
So, there's no one else?

00:19:29.750 --> 00:19:29.910
Bye!

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:30.460
What can I do?

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:33.480
In fact, I'm the only one who can.

00:19:35.180 --> 00:19:37.380
I'm going to do this using Death Note

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:39.100
I will change the world!

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:22.530
First, I wrote the names of the worst criminals I could remember, as if I cleaned the world one name at a time.

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:26.260
So that one day, no one will do anything wrong again.

00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:29.940
While the truly guilty, who deserve to be

00:20:30.030 --> 00:20:32.350
and those who are punished for their crimes die of cardiac arrest,

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:35.100
the less guilty people, but who still cause problems,

00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:37.620
will be gradually erased by accident or death.

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:43.000
So, and only then, the world will start moving in the right direction.

00:20:43.100 --> 00:20:44.900
It will be a new world free of...

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:49.400
and populated by people that I judged to be honest, kind and hardworking.

00:20:49.660 --> 00:20:53.480
But if you do that, you'll be the only bad person in the world.

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:56.690
Huh? I have no idea what you're talking about.

00:20:57.680 --> 00:20:59.960
I'm a great student of the Force, who is considered-

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:09.200
considered one of the best and brightest in Japan, and I, I will become the god of this new world.

